ptoms includes   Allergy to lidocaine  No   Medications anticoagulants  Patient is not on blood thinners     Social History  NA   Family History  NA    Past Medical History   Personal history of malignancy includes  Right breast Ca  DCIS LCIS and inv   ductal     Review of Patient Data in the EMR   Radiology  Yes   Past Histology  Yes   Office Notes  Yes     Physical Examination  Laterality was established according to departmental  universal protocol  Examination of the right breast reveals a 0 5cm  subcutaneous nodule lateral to the well healed areolar scar     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  written consent was obtained  2 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles  without anesthesia and without complications  1 slide was stained for immediate  evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were not discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to NP  Erin Keefe by text  message and in person at 12 o clock p m         The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Martha Bishop Pitman MD on REMOVED_DATE 15 15     Hormone Receptor Quantitation    QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS    Right Tram  cell block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2   See note       Note   Estrogen and p