Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Private Outside MGH MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Gabrielle Baker  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 78 year old woman with a history of IDC in the right breast diagnosis in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   S P radiation  tamoxifen  now with palpable mass in left breast and abnormal mammogram  BI RADD 5   now undergoing core biopsy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Sections of the core biopsy reveal infiltrating nests and cords of malignant epithelial cells with associated desmoplasia  The tumor cells are mostly small with increased nucleus to cytoplasm ratio and eccentrically placed nuclei  In some areas there is a prominent single file pattern suggesting a component of lobular differentiation  An immunohistochemical stain for e cadherin demonstrates focal weak staining in a minority of tumor cells  In the context of the morphologic findings  the immunohistochemical staining pattern suggests a component of lobular carcinoma or a poorly differentiated ductal carcinoma loss of expression of e cadherin  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected 